  "full_response": "**POLICE REPORT**\n**Case Number:** 2023-045789\n**Reporting Officer:** Detective Marcus R. Holloway (Badge #7421)\n**Date of Report:** October 12, 2023\n**Time of Report:** 14:30\n**Incident Type:** Grand Theft Auto (Felony)\n**Location of Incident:** 1247 Maplewood Drive, Riverside, CA 92501 (Parking lot of Riverside Plaza Shopping Center)\n\n---\n\n### **SUSPECT INFORMATION**\n**Full Name:** Jonathan Elias Whitmore\n**Date of Birth:** March 15, 1989 (Age: 34)\n**Driver’s License Number:** C98745621 (Issued: California, Expires: 03/15/2025)\n**Home Address:** 3428 Pinecrest Avenue, Apt. 204, Riverside, CA 92506\n**Phone Number:** (951) 555-0178\n**Physical Description:**\n- Height: 5’11”\n- Weight: 185 lbs\n- Hair: Brown (short, receding)\n- Eyes: Hazel\n- Distinguishing Features: Tattoo of a serpent on left forearm, scar above right eyebrow\n\n---\n\n### **NARRATIVE**\nAt approximately 13:45 on October 12, 2023, officers responded to a 911 call reporting a stolen vehicle from the Riverside Plaza Shopping Center. The victim, **Daniel R. Mercer (DOB: 07/22/1978)**, stated that his **2022 Tesla Model 3 (VIN: 5YJ3E1EB8NF123456, License Plate: 6TRJ321)** was taken from the parking lot while he was inside the grocery store for approximately 10 minutes.\n\nUpon reviewing security footage, officers observed a male suspect matching the description of **Jonathan Elias Whitmore** approaching the victim’s vehicle, using a device to bypass the electronic lock, and driving away in the Tesla. The suspect was last seen heading eastbound on Maplewood Drive.\n\nA BOLO (Be On the Lookout) was issued for the suspect and the stolen vehicle",
